    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** serving as our clear offensive anchor. With a score of 72.07, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable matchup against Phillips (4.52 xERA), providing the most reliable floor-ceiling combination in the lineup. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.70) also commands a strong start, as he draws a positive park factor and a soft matchup against Bradish. While **Gunnar Henderson** (58.62) and **Josh Jung** (59.95) are facing tougher arms in Miles and Pfaadt, respectively, their high-leverage spots in the order keep them firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier, ensuring we maintain our scoring momentum in R, HR, and RBI.\n\nThe optimization process was most difficult regarding the utility spot and the remaining bench depth. **Coby Mayo** (38.12) was the final player cut, narrowly failing to clear the 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. His proximity to the lineup is noted, but the combined pressure of an elite arm in Miles and an unfavorable platoon split pushed him off the roster in favor of the higher-floor profile of **Miguel Vargas** (46.59). Meanwhile, we are navigating a precarious situation with **Heliot Ramos** (58.15); while he profiles well against Thornton, the presence of an elite defensive catcher behind the plate creates a slight drag on his base-running upside, a critical metric for our scarcity-focused strategy.\n\nLooking ahead, we must continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, whose absence on the IL remains a significant drain on our overall output. We are effectively playing a man down in the high-impact slots, forcing us to lean heavily on the consistency of **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the order. With **Liam Hicks** (49.13) and **Drake Baldwin** (48.32) providing marginal utility, we are relying on our core trio of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** to carry the weight. Managers should keep a close watch on late-breaking weather or lineup changes, as any volatility could force a late shuffle to protect our limited game caps.",
